Na 3 V 2 O 1.6 (PO 4 ) 2 F 1.4  (NVOPF) with WC P-O bonds, which was synthesized by nonequilibrium fast calcination (NFC), was defined as WC/NFC-NVOPF. The NFC equipment with a temperature control system works by Joule thermal shock. The NFC equipment was purchased from Shenzhen Zhongkejingyan Company (HTS-1510D). The WC/NFC-NVOPF was prepared by mixing a stoichiometric proportion of Na 2 CO 3  (Macklin, ≥99.5%), NaF (Meryer, 99%), V 2 O 5  (Aladdin, 99%), NH 4 H 2 PO 4  (Aladdin, 99%) and 3 wt% excessive graphene (Sigma-Aldrich). Then, the mixture was then ball-milled at 300 rpm for 24 h with 5 mm agate grinding balls (ball-to-powder weight ratio of 10:1) in a ball-milling machine (Changsha Mitr Instrument Equipment Co., Ltd., YQXM-0.4 L). Each milling lasted for 1 h, with a 5 min intermittent rest times. Then the mixture was dried at 100 °C for 12 h. Finally, using 5 cm × \documentclass[12pt]{minimal}
